ProsperoSunshine: tell the platform which paired client a session's gamepads belong to

The PS5 host gives the host role (the console's user, PS and Create) to a paired device, not to a gamepad slot, so a
device that leaves and comes back gets it again and nobody inherits it (GitHub issue 15). alloc_gamepad only gets the
session's feedback queue, so stream::session::start() tells the platform once which client that queue belongs to,
through the new platf::set_gamepad_owner. The session holds the queue, so the mail hands out the same one to a resumed
input when it is rebound.

--- a/src/platform/common.h
+++ b/src/platform/common.h
@@ -1304,6 +1304,16 @@
    * @return 0 when the gamepad exists and was rebound; otherwise -1.
    */
   int rebind_gamepad(input_t &input, const gamepad_id_t &id, feedback_queue_t feedback_queue);
+
+  /**
+   * @brief Tell the platform which paired client a session's gamepad feedback queue belongs to.
+   *
+   * The PS5 host gives the host role (the console's user, PS and Create) to a paired device rather than to a gamepad slot.
+   *
+   * @param feedback_queue The session's feedback queue, the one alloc_gamepad later gets for its gamepads.
+   * @param owner The paired client's certificate.
+   */
+  void set_gamepad_owner(const feedback_queue_t &feedback_queue, std::string_view owner);
   /**
    * @brief Release gamepad resources.
